#: includes/mcp/class-server.php:178
msgid "Tools for WholesaleX, the wholesale and B2B extension of this WooCommerce store. Start with wholesalex-get-store-overview. Find product, category, customer, role and checkout IDs with the search and list tools before creating rules. Read settings with wholesalex-get-settings before changing them with wholesalex-update-settings; read-only settings must be changed by the store owner on the Settings screen. Changes apply to the live store: new rules start inactive unless active is true, so tell the store owner what you created, and confirm with them before deleting anything. Prices use the store currency, and dates use YYYY-MM-DD in the store timezone."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-server.php:178
msgid "Use the current tool schemas and settings to determine what MCP can actually do; never claim an unavailable action succeeded or substitute a different rule type."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-server.php:187
msgid "Use User Roles restrictions by default for ALL role restriction requests. Find the intended roles with wholesalex-list-roles, read each with wholesalex-get-role, then use wholesalex-update-role. With active licensed Pro, use product_visibility to hide products; non_purchasable to block purchases while keeping prices visible; checkout_restriction for matching cart quantity and order value limits or blocking checkout; price_visibility to hide prices and optionally show_request_quote; tax_rule for tax exemptions, countries and classes; replace_cart_with_quote for role-wide quote replacement; restrict_subaccount_creation to allow or block subaccount creation by role; general_excluded_customer_ids for general exemptions. For individual subaccount creation, use the separate Pro wholesalex-get-subaccount-options and wholesalex-create-subaccount tools when present. Resolve the parent customer, collect username, email, full name and requested permissions, and create only with the user's authorization. Never request or expose passwords; use the configured password-setup email. Editing and deleting individual subaccounts are unavailable. Do not claim an unavailable operation succeeded. disable_coupons is also available. Pro restriction fields are available only while Pro is active and compatible; check current schemas and related add-on settings. Preserve existing targets, exclusions and unrelated restrictions. If the audience is unspecified, ask which roles should be affected; never assume every role. Do not substitute matching-cart totals for per-product limits or claim unsupported behavior. Use pricing rule tools for wholesale prices and discounts. Dynamic rules are legacy: use dynamic rule tools only when the user explicitly requests dynamic rules or identifies an existing dynamic rule to manage. Do not proactively suggest or create dynamic rules, including as a fallback when a role restriction is unavailable."
msgstr ""

